---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import LegalIntro from '../components/LegalIntro.astro';
import Fact from '../components/Fact.astro';
import EmailLink from '../components/EmailLink.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'request', label: 'How to request deletion' },
  { id: 'verify', label: 'How we verify the request' },
  { id: 'deleted', label: 'What is deleted' },
  { id: 'kept', label: 'What we may keep' },
  { id: 'timeframe', label: 'How long it takes' },
  { id: 'status', label: 'Checking the status' },
  { id: 'disconnect', label: 'Disconnecting a Page or account' },
  { id: 'inactive', label: 'If you stop using Get Assist' },
  { id: 'customers', label: 'If you messaged a business' },
];
const l = site.legal;
---

<DocLayout
  title="Data deletion"
  description="How to ask Get Assist to delete your data, what is deleted, how long it takes, and what happens when a Facebook Page or Instagram account is disconnected."
  toc={toc}
>
  <div slot="intro">
    <LegalIntro title="Data deletion instructions">
      <p class="text-slate">
        To have your data deleted, email <EmailLink email={site.emails.privacy} /> with the subject
        “Data deletion request”. Workspace owners can also write to{' '}
        <EmailLink email={site.emails.support} />. You do not need a {site.brand} account to ask.
        The steps below explain what to include and what happens next.
      </p>
    </LegalIntro>
  </div>

  <h2 id="request">How to request deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Email <EmailLink email={site.emails.privacy} /> and include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name and the email address you use with {site.brand}, if you have an account;</li>
    <li>the workspace name, if you are a workspace owner;</li>
    <li>
      the Facebook Page name or Instagram username concerned, if your request is about a connected
      Page or account;
    </li>
    <li>
      if you messaged a business that uses {site.brand}: the name of that business, the channel
      (Messenger or Instagram) and the name or username you messaged from;
    </li>
    <li>what you want deleted: everything, or specific conversations or data.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Do not send passwords or payment details.</p>

  <h2 id="verify">How we verify the request</h2>
  <p>
    We delete data only for the person or business it belongs to. Requests to delete a workspace
    must come from an authorised workspace owner. Before deleting we may ask you to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>reply from the email address linked to the {site.brand} account; or</li>
    <li>
      show that you manage the Page or Instagram account concerned, for example by sending a message
      from it; or
    </li>
    <li>
      for people who messaged a business, confirm details of the conversation so we can find it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="deleted">What is deleted or anonymised</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Workspace requests: account profiles, team membership, settings and knowledge base content.
    </li>
    <li>
      Connected Page or account requests: access tokens, conversation messages, customer
      identifiers, attachments and notes for that Page or account.
    </li>
    <li>
      Requests from people who messaged a business: your messages, identifiers and attachments in
      that business’s inbox.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="kept">What we may keep</h2>
  <p>
    We may keep limited records where the law requires it, such as invoices and payment records, and
    a record that a deletion request was made and completed. Data in backups is removed as those
    backups expire: <Fact fact={site.retention.backups} />
  </p>

  <h2 id="timeframe">How long it takes</h2>
  <p>
    We confirm that we received your request, then delete or anonymise the data within{' '}
    <Fact fact={l.deletionTimeframe} /> of verifying it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="status">Checking the status of your request</h2>
  <p>
    We reply by email when the request is complete. You can also ask about the status at any time by
    replying to that email thread or writing to <EmailLink email={site.emails.privacy} />.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disconnect">When a Page or Instagram account is disconnected</h2>
  <p>
    Disconnecting and deleting are different. If a business disconnects a Page or Instagram account
    inside {site.brand}, or removes {site.brand} in its Facebook or Instagram settings, we stop
    receiving new messages for it straight away.
  </p>
  <p>
    Conversations already stored: <Fact fact={l.afterDisconnect} />
  </p>
  <p>
    When you remove {site.brand} in your Facebook settings: <Fact fact={l.metaDeletionCallback} />
  </p>

  <h2 id="inactive">If you stop using {site.brand}</h2>
  <p>
    Account data after a customer stops using {site.brand}: <Fact fact={site.retention.account} />
    You can ask us to delete it earlier at any time using the steps above.
  </p>

  <h2 id="customers">If you messaged a business that uses {site.brand}</h2>
  <p>
    The business you messaged controls your conversation data, and {site.brand} processes it on that
    business’s behalf. You can ask the business directly, or email{' '}
    <EmailLink email={site.emails.privacy} /> with the details above and we will handle the request
    with the business.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
